body:
Console renders blank on Vercel because `external: ['crypto']` in the Rollup config emits a bare `import 'crypto'` in the ESM bundle — browsers cannot resolve bare specifiers, so React never mounts.

## Root cause fix

Replaced `external: ['crypto']` with a Vite plugin that stubs `createHash`/`createVerify` at resolve time:

```ts
// scripts/vite-crypto-stub.ts
export function viteCryptoStub(): Plugin {
  return {
    name: 'stub-crypto',
    enforce: 'pre', // must run before vite:resolve browser-external
    resolveId(id) { if (id === 'crypto') return '\0crypto-stub'; },
    load(id) {
      if (id === '\0crypto-stub') {
        return 'export function createHash() { return { update() { return this; }, digest() { return ""; } }; }\nexport default {};';
      }
    },
  };
}
```

Applied to both `apps/console/vite.config.ts` and `examples/msw-todo/vite.config.ts`.

## E2E tests against production build

- **`playwright.config.ts`** — `webServer` now builds the console and serves via `vite preview` (port 4173), matching the Vercel deployment artifact
- **`e2e/smoke.spec.ts`** — 6 tests: uncaught JS errors, React `#root` mount, visible text, asset 404s, page title, app shell/loading screen visibility
- **`e2e/console-rendering.spec.ts`** — 4 tests: console.error monitoring, client-side route rendering, SPA fallback (deep routes return index.html), MSW service worker presence
- **`e2e/helpers/index.ts`** — shared `waitForReactMount` utility

## CI integration

- Added `e2e` job to `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (runs after `build`, Chromium only, uploads Playwright report on failure)

